            "title": "Why the Under-Layer Matters",
            "use_h1": false
          }
        },
        "body": {
          "type": "text",
          "settings": {
            "text": "<p>Most parents focus on the sleep bag TOG rating — but what baby wears underneath determines whether the system actually works. Cotton traps moisture against the skin. That's why a baby in a cotton onesie under their sleep bag wakes up damp, clammy, and uncomfortable at 2am.</p><p>TENCEL™ Lyocell solves this at the source. It's a botanic fiber made from eucalyptus wood pulp, and independent testing shows it absorbs moisture roughly <strong>50% more efficiently than cotton</strong>. It keeps wicking where cotton gives up — so your baby stays dry and comfortable for the full 10–12 hours they're in that garment.</p>",
            "enlarge_text": false
          }
        },
